; ==========================================================================
; Bouncing-Ball-v05  -  two 3x3 balls that bounce off each other, faster
; ==========================================================================
; v04 made faster. The balls, the bounces, the collision latch and the
; flicker-free stale-edge erase are all as before; what changed is how the
; frame reaches the screen. Measured in the simulator on V0061.34:
;
;   v04 69,313 1802 instructions + 151 bytes a frame; v05 22,275 + 121 (3.1x fewer)
;
; WHERE v04's TIME WENT. 41% of a frame was DIVXY splitting cursor positions
; into digits (13 cursor moves a frame, two divides each), and most of the rest
; was emitting bytes one SEROUTI at a time. So:
;  - the digits come from two 81-byte tables (READIDX) instead of dividing by ten
;  - a ball is drawn with ONE cursor move and ONE PRINTSTR of
;    ESC[7m, three spaces, three backspaces, ESC[B (down one line), ... ESC[0m
;    - v04 used three cursor moves and nine SEROUTIs. The stale column is erased
;    the same way.
;  - the collision test is TESTLXY (gap < 3) rather than dividing by three
;  - the vertical step is gated by a 6-frame phase table (6 = 1 x 2 x 3, the
;    three possible angles) instead of dividing a frame counter.
;
; ONE VISIBLE CHANGE: the balls now travel columns 2-79 (v04: 1-80). Writing in
; column 80 leaves a VT100's cursor parked ON column 80, and the backspace that
; follows would land one column short. Lines are still 1-23.
;
; REGISTERS. R0 the frame phase 0-5, R1-R5 ball A and R6-R10 ball B as x, y,
; x-direction, y-direction and the ball's row in the phase table (angle x 6),
; R11/R12 old x/y, R13 line and R14 column for POSXY, R15 a pointer.
; Data at $4900 past the end marker: banner, the latch ($4950), the phase
; table ($4960), the digit tables ($4980, $49E0) and the strings ($4A40).
;
; Built by Firmware-Math/build_ball5.py; checked by Firmware-Math/ball5_verify.py.
; Any key launches, ESC stops and tidies up. DLYI 04 near the end of the loop
; is the speed knob.
;
; HW-VERIFIED on the Elf2K (V0061.34), 2026-09-26 - Craig: "works great".
;
; 252 STELLAR commands, $4000-$42AC (685 bytes of code).
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; D 4000 CD             START                      Start of program, and run the label pre-pass
; D 4001 11 0F 09 00    LOADXI R15 0900            Point at the banner
; D 4005 C1 0F          PRINTSTR R15               Print it
; SEED:
; D 4007 C3             RAND                       Advance the generator - the count depends on the operator
; D 4008 CC             SERST                      Has a key arrived?
; D 4009 A1 00 07       IFFALSEI SEED              Not yet - go round again
; D 400C CB             SERIN                      Take the key and throw it away
; D 400D 51 00 00       SUBXYZ R0 - R0 -> R0       Frame phase, 0-5, starts at 0
; D 4010 11 0F 09 50    LOADXI R15 0950            The touching latch starts clear
; D 4014 32 0F 00 00    COPYMX2I R15 0000
; D 4018 11 01 00 22    LOADXI R1 0022             Ball A starts at column 34
; D 401C 11 02 00 0F    LOADXI R2 000F             line 15
; D 4020 11 06 00 2C    LOADXI R6 002C             Ball B starts at column 44
; D 4024 11 07 00 05    LOADXI R7 0005             and line 5
; D 4028 C3             RAND                       One random value drives both launches
; D 4029 21 0B          COPYAX Acc -> R11          Park it in R11
; D 402B 11 0C 00 02    LOADXI R12 0002            Two
; D 402F 4D BC          DIVXY R11 / R12            Divide the running random value
; D 4031 27             COPYREMA
; D 4032 21 03          COPYAX Acc -> R3           Ball A horizontal direction
; D 4034 25             COPYMAA                    Keep the quotient for the next one
; D 4035 21 0B          COPYAX Acc -> R11
; D 4037 4D BC          DIVXY R11 / R12            Divide the running random value
; D 4039 27             COPYREMA
; D 403A 21 04          COPYAX Acc -> R4           Ball A vertical direction
; D 403C 25             COPYMAA                    Keep the quotient for the next one
; D 403D 21 0B          COPYAX Acc -> R11
; D 403F 4D BC          DIVXY R11 / R12            Divide the running random value
; D 4041 27             COPYREMA
; D 4042 21 08          COPYAX Acc -> R8           Ball B horizontal direction
; D 4044 25             COPYMAA                    Keep the quotient for the next one
; D 4045 21 0B          COPYAX Acc -> R11
; D 4047 4D BC          DIVXY R11 / R12            Divide the running random value
; D 4049 27             COPYREMA
; D 404A 21 09          COPYAX Acc -> R9           Ball B vertical direction
; D 404C 25             COPYMAA                    Keep the quotient for the next one
; D 404D 21 0B          COPYAX Acc -> R11
; D 404F 11 0C 00 03    LOADXI R12 0003            Three
; D 4053 4D BC          DIVXY R11 / R12            Divide the running random value
; D 4055 27             COPYREMA
; D 4056 21 05          COPYAX Acc -> R5           Ball A angle, 0-2
; D 4058 25             COPYMAA                    Keep the quotient for the next one
; D 4059 21 0B          COPYAX Acc -> R11
; D 405B 4D BC          DIVXY R11 / R12            Divide the running random value
; D 405D 27             COPYREMA
; D 405E 21 0A          COPYAX Acc -> R10          Ball B angle, 0-2
; D 4060 25             COPYMAA                    Keep the quotient for the next one
; D 4061 21 0B          COPYAX Acc -> R11
; D 4063 50 55 0F       ADDXYZ R5 + R5 -> R15      Ball A: its row in the phase table is angle x 6
; D 4066 50 F5 0F       ADDXYZ R15 + R5 -> R15
; D 4069 50 FF 05       ADDXYZ R15 + R15 -> R5
; D 406C 50 AA 0F       ADDXYZ R10 + R10 -> R15    Ball B: its row in the phase table is angle x 6
; D 406F 50 FA 0F       ADDXYZ R15 + R10 -> R15
; D 4072 50 FF 0A       ADDXYZ R15 + R15 -> R10
; D 4075 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B                 ESC
; D 4077 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B '['             [
; D 4079 CA 32          SEROUTI 32 '2'             2
; D 407B CA 4A          SEROUTI 4A 'J'             J - clear the screen
; D 407D CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B                 ESC
; D 407F CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B '['             [
; D 4081 CA 3F          SEROUTI 3F '?'             ?
; D 4083 CA 32          SEROUTI 32 '2'             2
; D 4085 CA 35          SEROUTI 35 '5'             5
; D 4087 CA 6C          SEROUTI 6C 'l'             l - hide the cursor
; D 4089 23 00 1E       COPYXY R1 -> R14
; D 408C 23 00 2D       COPYXY R2 -> R13
; D 408F BD 02 67       CALL DRAW                  Put ball A on the screen
; D 4092 23 00 6E       COPYXY R6 -> R14
; D 4095 23 00 7D       COPYXY R7 -> R13
; D 4098 BD 02 67       CALL DRAW                  and ball B
; LOOP:
; D 409B 42 00          INCX R0                    Next frame phase
; D 409D 86 00 00 06    TESTXI R0 0006
; D 40A1 A1 00 A8       IFFALSEI PH
; D 40A4 53 00 00 06    SUBXI R0 0006              wrapping 5 -> 0
; PH:
; D 40A8 45 16          SUBXY R1 - R6              How far apart horizontally?
; D 40AA 25             COPYMAA                    The magnitude
; D 40AB 21 0B          COPYAX Acc -> R11
; D 40AD 11 0C 00 03    LOADXI R12 0003            Three - the ball's width
; D 40B1 89 BC          TESTLXY R11 < R12          Under three?
; D 40B3 A1 00 E9       IFFALSEI NOHIT             No - clear of each other
; D 40B6 45 27          SUBXY R2 - R7              How far apart vertically?
; D 40B8 25             COPYMAA                    The magnitude
; D 40B9 21 0B          COPYAX Acc -> R11
; D 40BB 89 BC          TESTLXY R11 < R12          Under three?
; D 40BD A1 00 E9       IFFALSEI NOHIT             No - clear vertically, so no collision
; D 40C0 11 0F 09 50    LOADXI R15 0950            Point at the touching latch
; D 40C4 33 0F          COPYMXA 0F                 Read it
; D 40C6 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000                Were they apart last frame?
; D 40C9 A1 00 DE       IFFALSEI LATCH             No - already bounced, leave them alone
; D 40CC 23 00 3B       COPYXY R3 -> R11           Save ball A's horizontal direction
; D 40CF 23 00 83       COPYXY R8 -> R3            Ball A takes ball B's
; D 40D2 23 00 B8       COPYXY R11 -> R8           and ball B takes ball A's
; D 40D5 23 00 4B       COPYXY R4 -> R11           The same for the vertical directions
; D 40D8 23 00 94       COPYXY R9 -> R4
; D 40DB 23 00 B9       COPYXY R11 -> R9
; LATCH:
; D 40DE 11 0F 09 50    LOADXI R15 0950            Remember that they are touching
; D 40E2 32 0F 00 01    COPYMX2I R15 0001
; D 40E6 B0 00 F1       GAL HITDONE
; NOHIT:
; D 40E9 11 0F 09 50    LOADXI R15 0950            They are apart - clear the latch
; D 40ED 32 0F 00 00    COPYMX2I R15 0000
; HITDONE:
; D 40F1 23 00 1B       COPYXY R1 -> R11           Remember where this ball is
; D 40F4 23 00 2C       COPYXY R2 -> R12
; D 40F7 86 03 00 00    TESTXI R3 0000             Heading right?
; D 40FB A1 01 12       IFFALSEI XLA               No - heading left
; D 40FE 42 01          INCX R1                    x = x + 1
; D 4100 86 01 00 4E    TESTXI R1 004E             Would the right edge pass column 79?
; D 4104 A1 01 23       IFFALSEI XDA               No - carry on
; D 4107 11 01 00 4C    LOADXI R1 004C             Reflect to 76
; D 410B 11 03 00 01    LOADXI R3 0001             and bounce - now heading left
; D 410F B0 01 23       GAL XDA
; XLA:
; D 4112 43 01          DECX R1                    x = x - 1
; D 4114 86 01 00 01    TESTXI R1 0001             Reached column 1?
; D 4118 A1 01 23       IFFALSEI XDA               No - carry on
; D 411B 11 01 00 03    LOADXI R1 0003             Reflect to 3
; D 411F 11 03 00 00    LOADXI R3 0000             and bounce - now heading right
; XDA:
; D 4123 50 50 0F       ADDXYZ R5 + R0 -> R15      This ball's row + the frame phase
; D 4126 2E 0F 09 60    READIDX R15 0960           Is this a frame for its vertical step?
; D 412A 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 412D A0 01 5A       IFTRUEI SYA                No - leave y alone this time
; D 4130 86 04 00 00    TESTXI R4 0000             Heading down?
; D 4134 A1 01 4B       IFFALSEI YUA               No - heading up
; D 4137 42 02          INCX R2                    y = y + 1
; D 4139 86 02 00 16    TESTXI R2 0016             Would the bottom edge pass line 23?
; D 413D A1 01 5A       IFFALSEI SYA               No - carry on
; D 4140 11 02 00 14    LOADXI R2 0014             Reflect to 20
; D 4144 11 04 00 01    LOADXI R4 0001             and bounce - now heading up
; D 4148 B0 01 5A       GAL SYA
; YUA:
; D 414B 43 02          DECX R2                    y = y - 1
; D 414D 8C 02          TESTXZ R2                  Reached line 0?
; D 414F A1 01 5A       IFFALSEI SYA               No - carry on
; D 4152 11 02 00 02    LOADXI R2 0002             Reflect to 2
; D 4156 11 04 00 00    LOADXI R4 0000             and bounce - now heading down
; SYA:
; D 415A 88 1B          TESTGXY R1 >= R11          Did x increase?
; D 415C A1 01 65       IFFALSEI ELA               No - the stale column is on the right
; D 415F 23 00 BE       COPYXY R11 -> R14          Moving right: the old left edge is stale
; D 4162 B0 01 6C       GAL ECA
; ELA:
; D 4165 23 00 BE       COPYXY R11 -> R14          Moving left: the old right edge is stale
; D 4168 52 0E 00 02    ADDXI R14 0002
; ECA:
; D 416C 23 00 CD       COPYXY R12 -> R13          From the old top line
; D 416F BD 02 72       CALL POSXY
; D 4172 11 0F 0A 5E    LOADXI R15 0A5E
; D 4176 C1 0F          PRINTSTR R15               Blank the stale column, top to bottom
; D 4178 87 2C          TESTXY R2 = R12            Did y stay put this frame?
; D 417A A0 01 9B       IFTRUEI NRA                Yes - nothing more to erase
; D 417D 88 2C          TESTGXY R2 >= R12          Did y increase?
; D 417F A1 01 88       IFFALSEI EUA               No - the stale row is the old bottom
; D 4182 23 00 CD       COPYXY R12 -> R13          Moving down: the old top row is stale
; D 4185 B0 01 8F       GAL ERA
; EUA:
; D 4188 23 00 CD       COPYXY R12 -> R13          Moving up: the old bottom row is stale
; D 418B 52 0D 00 02    ADDXI R13 0002
; ERA:
; D 418F 23 00 BE       COPYXY R11 -> R14          From the old left edge
; D 4192 BD 02 72       CALL POSXY
; D 4195 11 0F 0A 6A    LOADXI R15 0A6A
; D 4199 C1 0F          PRINTSTR R15               Three spaces clear the row
; NRA:
; D 419B 23 00 6B       COPYXY R6 -> R11           Remember where this ball is
; D 419E 23 00 7C       COPYXY R7 -> R12
; D 41A1 86 08 00 00    TESTXI R8 0000             Heading right?
; D 41A5 A1 01 BC       IFFALSEI XLB               No - heading left
; D 41A8 42 06          INCX R6                    x = x + 1
; D 41AA 86 06 00 4E    TESTXI R6 004E             Would the right edge pass column 79?
; D 41AE A1 01 CD       IFFALSEI XDB               No - carry on
; D 41B1 11 06 00 4C    LOADXI R6 004C             Reflect to 76
; D 41B5 11 08 00 01    LOADXI R8 0001             and bounce - now heading left
; D 41B9 B0 01 CD       GAL XDB
; XLB:
; D 41BC 43 06          DECX R6                    x = x - 1
; D 41BE 86 06 00 01    TESTXI R6 0001             Reached column 1?
; D 41C2 A1 01 CD       IFFALSEI XDB               No - carry on
; D 41C5 11 06 00 03    LOADXI R6 0003             Reflect to 3
; D 41C9 11 08 00 00    LOADXI R8 0000             and bounce - now heading right
; XDB:
; D 41CD 50 A0 0F       ADDXYZ R10 + R0 -> R15     This ball's row + the frame phase
; D 41D0 2E 0F 09 60    READIDX R15 0960           Is this a frame for its vertical step?
; D 41D4 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 41D7 A0 02 04       IFTRUEI SYB                No - leave y alone this time
; D 41DA 86 09 00 00    TESTXI R9 0000             Heading down?
; D 41DE A1 01 F5       IFFALSEI YUB               No - heading up
; D 41E1 42 07          INCX R7                    y = y + 1
; D 41E3 86 07 00 16    TESTXI R7 0016             Would the bottom edge pass line 23?
; D 41E7 A1 02 04       IFFALSEI SYB               No - carry on
; D 41EA 11 07 00 14    LOADXI R7 0014             Reflect to 20
; D 41EE 11 09 00 01    LOADXI R9 0001             and bounce - now heading up
; D 41F2 B0 02 04       GAL SYB
; YUB:
; D 41F5 43 07          DECX R7                    y = y - 1
; D 41F7 8C 07          TESTXZ R7                  Reached line 0?
; D 41F9 A1 02 04       IFFALSEI SYB               No - carry on
; D 41FC 11 07 00 02    LOADXI R7 0002             Reflect to 2
; D 4200 11 09 00 00    LOADXI R9 0000             and bounce - now heading down
; SYB:
; D 4204 88 6B          TESTGXY R6 >= R11          Did x increase?
; D 4206 A1 02 0F       IFFALSEI ELB               No - the stale column is on the right
; D 4209 23 00 BE       COPYXY R11 -> R14          Moving right: the old left edge is stale
; D 420C B0 02 16       GAL ECB
; ELB:
; D 420F 23 00 BE       COPYXY R11 -> R14          Moving left: the old right edge is stale
; D 4212 52 0E 00 02    ADDXI R14 0002
; ECB:
; D 4216 23 00 CD       COPYXY R12 -> R13          From the old top line
; D 4219 BD 02 72       CALL POSXY
; D 421C 11 0F 0A 5E    LOADXI R15 0A5E
; D 4220 C1 0F          PRINTSTR R15               Blank the stale column, top to bottom
; D 4222 87 7C          TESTXY R7 = R12            Did y stay put this frame?
; D 4224 A0 02 45       IFTRUEI NRB                Yes - nothing more to erase
; D 4227 88 7C          TESTGXY R7 >= R12          Did y increase?
; D 4229 A1 02 32       IFFALSEI EUB               No - the stale row is the old bottom
; D 422C 23 00 CD       COPYXY R12 -> R13          Moving down: the old top row is stale
; D 422F B0 02 39       GAL ERB
; EUB:
; D 4232 23 00 CD       COPYXY R12 -> R13          Moving up: the old bottom row is stale
; D 4235 52 0D 00 02    ADDXI R13 0002
; ERB:
; D 4239 23 00 BE       COPYXY R11 -> R14          From the old left edge
; D 423C BD 02 72       CALL POSXY
; D 423F 11 0F 0A 6A    LOADXI R15 0A6A
; D 4243 C1 0F          PRINTSTR R15               Three spaces clear the row
; NRB:
; D 4245 23 00 1E       COPYXY R1 -> R14           Both moved and erased: now draw both
; D 4248 23 00 2D       COPYXY R2 -> R13
; D 424B BD 02 67       CALL DRAW
; D 424E 23 00 6E       COPYXY R6 -> R14
; D 4251 23 00 7D       COPYXY R7 -> R13
; D 4254 BD 02 67       CALL DRAW
; D 4257 CC             SERST                      A key waiting?
; D 4258 A1 02 62       IFFALSEI NOKEY             No
; D 425B CB             SERIN                      Read it
; D 425C 81 00 1B       TESTAI 001B                Was it ESC?
; D 425F A0 02 90       IFTRUEI QUIT               Yes - stop
; NOKEY:
; D 4262 C0 04          DLYI 04                    Pace the animation
; D 4264 B0 00 9B       GAL LOOP                   Round again
; DRAW:
; D 4267 BD 02 72       CALL POSXY
; D 426A 11 0F 0A 40    LOADXI R15 0A40
; D 426E C1 0F          PRINTSTR R15               Reverse video, three rows of three, normal video
; D 4270 BE 00          RETURN
; POSXY:
; D 4272 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B                 ESC
; D 4274 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B '['             [
; D 4276 2E 0D 09 80    READIDX R13 0980           Line: tens digit
; D 427A C9             SEROUT
; D 427B 2E 0D 09 E0    READIDX R13 09E0           units digit
; D 427F C9             SEROUT
; D 4280 CA 3B          SEROUTI 3B ';'             ;
; D 4282 2E 0E 09 80    READIDX R14 0980           Column: tens digit
; D 4286 C9             SEROUT
; D 4287 2E 0E 09 E0    READIDX R14 09E0           units digit
; D 428B C9             SEROUT
; D 428C CA 48          SEROUTI 48 'H'             H
; D 428E BE 00          RETURN
; QUIT:
; D 4290 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B                 ESC
; D 4292 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B '['             [
; D 4294 CA 3F          SEROUTI 3F '?'             ?
; D 4296 CA 32          SEROUTI 32 '2'             2
; D 4298 CA 35          SEROUTI 35 '5'             5
; D 429A CA 68          SEROUTI 68 'h'             h - show the cursor again
; D 429C CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B                 ESC
; D 429E CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B '['             [
; D 42A0 CA 32          SEROUTI 32 '2'             2
; D 42A2 CA 4A          SEROUTI 4A 'J'             J
; D 42A4 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B                 ESC
; D 42A6 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B '['             [
; D 42A8 CA 48          SEROUTI 48 'H'             H - cursor home
; D 42AA F0 00 00       BREAK                      End of program

